---
description: Coverage work may fix in-scope bugs; never touch out-of-scope code
alwaysApply: true
---

When adding tests or driving toward coverage in `kramli-cli`:

**Allowed and encouraged**

- Patch production code in your assigned module when tests expose bugs, panics, deadlocks, or hangs.
- Add a failing test that documents correct behavior, then fix the implementation so it passes.
- Add minimal test hooks in the module under test when needed to hit error paths.

**Not allowed**

- Work around production bugs in tests only (weaker asserts, skips, ignored tests) to hit a coverage number.
- Refactor, reformat, or edit modules outside your task scope.
- Drive-by changes to unrelated files, dependencies, or CI.

**Tests**

- Use `#[kramli_test_macros::test]` / `#[kramli_test_macros::tokio_test]` (never bare `#[test]`).
- Descriptive test names; no `cov_*` prefix.
- Never nest `with_env_vars_async`.

See `AGENTS.md` → “Test coverage and bug discovery” for full conventions.
